  "question": {
    "text": "A small steel ball is dropped into a long cylinder containing glycerine. Which one of the following is the correct representation of the velocity time graph for the transit of the ball?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot1_0024_bb532e7e0c71.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 187px;\"/>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot2_0024_7b5fbf907b1d.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 186px;\"/>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot3_0024_6904320b8f03.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 185px;\"/>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img src=\"assets\\ot4_0024_151c19731e73.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 187px;\"/>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Consider a small steel ball as shown below:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0024_14e91c4c6928.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 182px;\"/></p><p>As shown in diagram, buoyancy force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>F</mi></math>.</p><p>Applying Newton's second law, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, then we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>v</mi></math></p><p>Integrating both sides, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mi>ln</mi><msup><msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>v</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Clearly, option B matches with the given variation of velocity with time.</p>"
